{"id":"chatcmpl-e8ab8c05-540d-45c0-9447-b2835b5af184","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244677,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first strategy for binary medical image findings: consult a domain expert tool for a direct comparison, then independently confirm with a grounded localization tool before committing to an answer. The key insight is cross-validating the same claim through two different tool modalities (expert reasoning vs. spatial grounding) to reduce error. The pattern generalizes to any forced-choice visual question where a single ambiguous feature determines the answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a binary choice hinges on one spatial/relational feature (e.g., which side is higher), first ask an expert tool to make the explicit comparison rather than guessing from the image.\",\n    \"Independently verify the leading hypothesis using a second, differently-grounded tool (localization/grounding) before finalizing the answer.\",\n    \"Use phrase grounding on the specific candidate finding to confirm it matches the correct side/location, converting a verbal claim into spatial evidence.\",\n    \"Resolve forced-choice questions by eliminating the alternative: confirm the positive finding's location, which implicitly rules out the other option.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging multiple-choice\": \"Ask an expert tool for the discriminating comparison first; then confirm with a grounding/localization tool on the specific candidate finding.\",\n    \"Binary spatial/relational questions\": \"Identify the single feature that separates the options, query it explicitly, and verify its location with an independent method.\",\n    \"Cross-validation of tool outputs\": \"Prefer answers supported by two independent tool modalities (reasoning + grounding) over a single source.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the discriminating feature (e.g., elevated side) was explicitly compared, not inferred.\",\n    \"Confirm a second independent tool localized the finding to the same side/location before answering.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":479,"total_tokens":857,"completion_tokens":378,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":479},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":378}}}